# Code ownership for Agent Portfolio Workbench.
#
# STATUS: informational / future-ready. The `main-protection` ruleset does NOT enable
# "Require review from Code Owners" while the repo is solo-maintained (GitHub forbids
# self-approval, so an active code-owner requirement would block the sole maintainer's
# own PRs). These entries stage the ownership map so the switch can be enabled with one
# ruleset change once at least one independent reviewer exists.
# See docs/github-governance.md and docs/reports/github-main-protection-readback-2026-07-21.md.
#
# Ownership assignment is a Human-Owned Decision under AGENTS.md. Replace the solo
# maintainer with an approved team when ownership is formalized.

# Default owner for everything not matched by a more specific rule below.
* @svandersloot

# High-risk paths — supply chain, automation, and machine-checkable contracts.
# These are the paths most likely to change security posture, CI behavior, or the
# guarantees other tooling relies on, so they get first-class review once code-owner
# review is activated.
/.github/workflows/** @svandersloot
/scripts/**          @svandersloot
/.claude/hooks/**    @svandersloot
/config/**           @svandersloot
/schemas/**          @svandersloot
